# Wave H.o — Operator shell TypeScript names

## Problem

DOM attrs are largely neutralized (H.l–H.n), but **shell TypeScript** still brands platform helpers as Denali:

| Symbol | Why wrong |
| ------ | --------- |
| `resolveDenaliDraftConflictStrategy` | Draft-engine conflict mode — workspace-neutral |
| `createDenaliDraftOnPushSuccess` | Tombstone shadow logger — workspace-neutral |
| `CreateTourWizardDenaliHeader` | Create-wizard chrome header used by operator shell |
| `showDenaliFullTemplate` | Means “extended create template plugins”, not Denali-only |

These are false product coupling: names imply Denali while logic is host/platform.

## Decision

| Before | After |
| ------ | ----- |
| `resolveDenaliDraftConflictStrategy` | `resolveOperatorDraftConflictStrategy` |
| `createDenaliDraftOnPushSuccess` | `createOperatorDraftOnPushSuccess` |
| `CreateTourWizardDenaliHeader` | `CreateTourWizardHeader` |
| `DenaliDraftSyncChrome` | `OperatorDraftSyncChrome` |
| `showDenaliFullTemplate` | `showExtendedWizardTemplate` |

Update all `apps/web` call sites + specs in lockstep (no deprecated aliases — closed rename).

## Out of scope

- `apps/web/src/wizard/denali/*` firewall (`resolveDenaliSyncWorkspacePlugin`, adapters re-exports)
- Generated draft-shell bindings (`getDenaliWorkspacePluginFromDraftShell`, …)
- Package `@app-tour/workspace-denali` export names
- Datetime/date-picker BEM → [`wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc`](./wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc) (Wave H.p)
- Install-graph isolation

## Verify

```bash
rg 'resolveDenaliDraftConflictStrategy|createDenaliDraftOnPushSuccess|CreateTourWizardDenaliHeader|showDenaliFullTemplate' \
  apps/web --glob '!**/*.generated.*'
# expect empty
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-h-operator-shell-ts-names.spec.ts \
  test/draft-unification-v3.spec.ts \
  test/denali-draft-unification-closure.spec.ts \
  test/create-page-split.spec.ts \
  test/wizard-host-boundary.spec.ts
```
